  "notes": "One level of Strassen's algorithm over 2 x 2 blocks of size H = ceil(N/2): seven identical H x H multiply-accumulate engines compute the seven block products from pre-sums of A and B formed one column (row) per step, and C is written once from the four post-sums, wrapping at AccW bits. Odd N pads the shared index with zeros and drops the padded output row and column. 7*H^2 multipliers (28 at N = 4), no eighth block product. Latency ceil(N/2) + 2 (4 at N = 4). Some flat registers have more than 2^31 bits near the edge of the parameter range.",
  "player": "septblock",
